Adding to the issue above, often times when you select a block of text, it copies the hashed (ig) version of that in the input and as you type if overrides it. Add before/after examples @simonklee 

<img width="1127" height="76" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2992ca6f-d405-49cd-823e-7e881e3b1dfb" /> {After}

<img width="1231" height="187" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eac59b6c-bf57-4b4f-8df7-0845a81f6a1f" /> {Before}

Which could take same effect via `opencode.json`, reference to [docs](https://opencode.ai/docs/models/): 
```json
{
  "provider": {
    "deepseek": {
      "models": {
        "deepseek-v4-flash": {
          "options": {
            "thinking": {
              "type": "disabled",
            },
          }
        },
        "deepseek-v4-pro": {
          "variants": {
            "thinking": {
              "thinking": {
                "type": "enabled"
              },
            },
            "nothinking": {
              "thinking": {
                "type": "disabled"
              },
            },
          },
        },
      }
    },
  },
  ...
}
```
Which means your can define options directly or custom variants. Feel free close issue.
